  "authors": [],
  "hashAlgorithm": "blake2b-256",
  "body": {
    "givenName": "Marco Vilgon",
    "image": {
      "@type": "ImageObject",
      "contentUrl": "",
      "sha256": "735c89e05b587497c92fa6ebac3eef7731938fab60576b8b6e6fe6871f5afb5b"
    },
    "motivations": "My motivation stems from the contrast between my reality in LatAm and my professional background. Living in Latin America, the need for censorship-resistant, frictionless financial rails isn't theoretical; it's an urgent necessity. Meanwhile, managing complex projects within S&P 500 companies taught me that great tech only survives if backed by rigorous execution and a solid business model. I want to bridge this gap. I'm stepping up as a DRep to inject a Lean Startup mentality into our governance. I want to use my corporate experience to demand accountability, ensuring that builders deliver on their promises and that our ecosystem aggressively transitions from a \"research phase\" to an \"execution and mass adoption phase.\"",
    "objectives": "I believe the success of Cardano relies on achieving true Product-Market Fit (PMF) beyond speculation. My objective as a DRep is to ensure the Treasury funds long-term infrastructure, Zero-Knowledge (ZK) privacy tools, and Real-World Asset (RWA) integrations that drive direct ROI to the network's P&L. I will vote to support projects that build scalable tech designed to make traditional intermediaries obsolete—aligning with Satoshi’s original peer-to-peer vision—while pushing for enterprise-grade adoption. I aim to block \"vaporware\" and short-term narratives, focusing our resources on sustainable frameworks that establish Cardano as the true financial operating system for the next decade.",
    "qualifications": "Corporate Rigor & Project Management: Extensive experience managing cross-functional projects and driving P&L optimization for S&P 500 enterprises. I bring corporate accountability to decentralized treasuries.\n\nAI-Powered Due Diligence: Proficient in Python and Data Science. I leverage Gen AI workflows to rapidly audit technical proposals, analyze architectures, and perform scale-level due diligence on Governance actions.\n\nWeb3 Infrastructure Knowledge: Deep understanding of blockchain architectures, ZK proofs (Midnight), and algorithmic mechanisms. I don't just read proposals; I understand the technical bottlenecks.\n\nLatAm Market Insight: First-hand experience with the economic realities of emerging markets, providing an edge in evaluating RWA and DeFi solutions built for real-world utility."
  }
}